# The creed, enforced rather than promised: nothing on this page may reach an
# origin that is not this one. `default-src 'none'` means every fetch the page
# could make is denied unless named below, and none of them may leave the host.
#
# The hash is of the medium script in the head, which is inline because it has
# to run before first paint and cannot afford a round trip. 404.html carries
# the same script byte for byte so one hash covers both; if you edit it, edit
# both and recompute:
#   python3 -c "import re,hashlib,base64;s=re.search(r'<script>(.*?)</script>',open('index.html').read(),re.S).group(1);print(base64.b64encode(hashlib.sha256(s.encode()).digest()).decode())"
